WEBVTT

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:05.830
The bitter memory of my childhood where I wasn't able to do a hip circle.

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:10.010
I almost gave up because I was exhausted and my hands were hurting.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:12.930
But, at that moment a girl whom I didn't know gave me a piece of caramel.

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:17.330
Her caramel was sweet and the flavour lifted my spirits.

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:23.030
But I was really surprised that the girl back then was actually our homeroom teacher, Yuzuki-sensei.

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:27.430
But sensei, why do you give out those caramels?

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:29.630
Is there a reason behind it?

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:35.640
<b>The Secret Mail Box</b>

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:32.820
Morning! 
-Morning!

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:35.610
Shuri-chan, is your body okay already?

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:40.810
Physically, I'm healthy as a horse.

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:43.270
It was only my head that was hurting.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.100
What have you been telling them?!

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.960
You know I didn't say anything!

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.370
Yes, yes, I know.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.920
What's wrong? You don't look too good.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:00.980
Nah, I had a long phone conversation just right after I got out of the bath yesterday.

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:03.040
So, I think I got something like a cold.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:07.740
You have to take care of your health, you know?

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:10.760
The only property of a person is their body.

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:14.290
Property, property, property.

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:19.410
Cake goes better with tepid red tea.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:21.820
What am I saying?

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:23.130
Right?

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.610
No idea.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.710
Ah, morning, Nanaka.

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:45.360
Hey, wait up.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:49.250
You're going to the committee meeting, right?
Let's go together if you are.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.250
<b>Library</b>

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:55.800
You've been angry ever since early this morning.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.960
I'm not angry.

00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:59.780
You are.

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:05.140
You didn't reply when I greeted you. And you had lunch by yourself.

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:06.840
You're definitely angry.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:09.030
I said I'm not angry!

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:19.140
Just leave me alone. If you're going to the committee meeting, then just go by yourself first.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:21.880
But, you really are angry, aren't you?

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:30.960
What's wrong? If I did something to make you mad, then tell me and I'll apologise.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:36.930
Last Saturday night, you were hugging Hoshino-san nearby the temple, weren't you?

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:40.820
You saw that?

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:41.750
I saw.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:46.950
That was because she was feeling light headed and about to collapse. I had no choice.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:51.130
It was something like an accident.

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:56.080
Remember during the festival night behind the temple, you got frightened by a raccoon...

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:58.190
...and you held me, right?

00:02:58.190 --> 00:03:01.070
Similarly, that was merely an accident.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:02.830
Accident?

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:08.550
That's right, an honest accident.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:12.950
So, the truth is, there's nothing going on between me and Hoshino-san.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:17.890
Enough.

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:20.600
I said that's enough!

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:28.760
Anyway, please don't bother me any further.

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:40.360
<b>Audio/Visual Room</b>

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:42.660
Hidaka-kun.

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:45.880
Hoshino-san.

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:48.370
Thank you for coming with me on Saturday.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:51.840
Not at all. It's nothing to be thankful about.

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:54.290
We can go again next time if you'd like.

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:56.910
Sure, if I'm free.

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:03.160
Would you cut it out?!

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:07.810
I already told you that it was an accident and a misunderstanding. Why do you keep twisting the facts?

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:16.440
Why? Why have you become like this?

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:22.140
The Nanaka I knew in the past isn't the Nanaka I know now!

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:26.290
Even you, Sana...

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:29.670
Haven't you changed as well, Sana?!

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:52.110
<i>What's with Nanaka?</i>

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:53.930
<i>I already told her that it was a misunderstanding.</i>

00:04:59.510 --> 00:05:01.200
<i>Did I say too much?</i>

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:18.340
<i>Regardless, Nanaka didn't have to behave like that.</i>

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:27.580
<i>The Nanaka I knew in the past was never like that.</i>

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:30.120
<i>She would always follow me wherever I went.</i>

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:33.350
<i>And, rather, I always had to help her.</i>

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:38.060
<i>We held hands whenever we passed a house with a scary dog.</i>

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:42.160
<i>And during lunch at school, I would even eat the carrots which she hated.</i>

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.870
<i>Also, that time too.</i>

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:53.080
Sana-chan, this mail box is no longer in use, is it?

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:56.340
That's why this is gonna become our mail box.

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:59.300
Huh? Ours?

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.050
That should do it.

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:14.880
Say, what do we do with our mail box?

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:23.460
We have things we don't want others to know, but kept and discussed amongst ourselves, right?

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:27.820
For that, we can write secret letters and put them inside here.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.000
And...

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:33.270
For you.

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:40.590
This is?

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:45.440
As long as we have these keys, we can open the mail box.

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:48.020
And we'll be able to secretly exchange letters.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:54.310
This is our very own secret, okay, Nanaka?

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:57.770
Our very own secret.

00:06:58.550 --> 00:07:00.820
You mustn't tell Shuu, Shuri and the others.

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:20.780
<b>{fs40\move(308,429,305,360,0,1910)}To: Sana</b>

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:20.900
<b>To: Sana</b>

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:21.030
<b>To: Sana</b>

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:21.260
<b>From: Nanaka</b>

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:21.380
<b>From: Nanaka</b>

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:22.330
<b>From: Nanaka</b>

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:30.250
Dear Sana-chan, this is a secret letter.

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:35.660
I had a nightmare yesterday and I woke up in the middle of the night.

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:39.550
When I closed my eyes, everything in front of me was so dark and I was so scared.

00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:42.150
I couldn't get back to sleep after that.

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:46.650
I have a feeling that I'm going to have the same dream again tonight and I'm really scared.

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:51.090
Dear Nanaka-chan, I read your secret letter.

00:07:51.090 --> 00:07:54.170
I have nightmares too once in a while.

00:07:54.170 --> 00:07:57.180
But, since I'm a guy, I'm fine.

00:07:57.180 --> 00:08:01.570
Since you're a girl, I guess you can't help but be scared.

00:08:01.570 --> 00:08:03.730
So, I'm going to give you a charm.

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:08.500
It's a stone I picked up in the river, but it's white, smooth and really cool.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:13.680
If you take this with you while you sleep, I'm sure you won't have anymore nightmares.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:19.450
Now, I (Sana) have no more problems with nightmares, but I hate the horizontal bar.

00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:23.130
There will be a a horizontal bar test during the next P.E. class...

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:27.910
...so, I'm practicising to be able to do a hip circle before then.

00:08:27.910 --> 00:08:32.640
Not being able to do a hip circle in front of everyone is embarrassing...

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:35.640
...so, I'm frantically trying my best.

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:45.620
Dear Sana-chan, the charm you gave me really worked.

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:51.070
Just like you said, I did not have anymore nightmares after going to sleep with it.

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:55.040
I'll always treasure the charm you gave me.

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:58.210
Also, work hard on your hip circle practice.

00:08:58.210 --> 00:09:00.920
You have all my support!

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:08.990
<i>Come to think of it, where did I put that mail box key?</i>

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:25.290
<i>I clearly remember having it when I moved.</i>

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:27.470
<i>What's left is...</i>

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:44.250
<i>Sana-chan, I made too much dinner, so I brought some for you...</i>

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:52.910
Sorry!
-Aoi-chan!

00:09:57.520 --> 00:09:58.540
There it is!

00:10:18.570 --> 00:10:20.180
What is this?

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:23.270
<b>HELP ME!{Full Length}</b>

00:10:23.730 --> 00:10:26.600
What the hell is this?!

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:30.990
<b>HELP ME!{Full Length}</b>

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:44.820
Sorry, the cleaning took longer than expected.

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:47.650
But, why did you ask me to come all the way here?

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:52.560
Don't tell me... "Actually, I love you."

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:56.190
Don't come up with such a corny confession please.

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:58.480
I don't swing that way.

00:10:58.480 --> 00:11:00.630
Shuu, regarding Nanaka.

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:03.600
What happened to Nanaka in the past?

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:08.200
What happened while I wasn't here?

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:12.420
What are you saying? Lots of things happened.

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:15.050
She's a ripe-aged girl after all.

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:16.820
Answer me seriously!

00:11:18.430 --> 00:11:19.370
Sorry...

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:22.780
Three years ago from today...

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:25.820
...when we were in Year 2 of middle school...

00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:27.880
...there was a fire at Nanaka's house.

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:30.130
Fire?!

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:34.150
I'm not certain, but it seems that it was arson.

00:11:34.150 --> 00:11:39.350
There was an investigation, but the arsonist was never found.

00:11:39.940 --> 00:11:44.090
In the fire, both of Nanaka's parents...

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:45.990
It can't be!

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:51.060
When the fire spread, Nanaka was asleep in her own room on the second floor.

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:54.780
Carrying only her violin, she jumped from her room in an instant.

00:11:59.770 --> 00:12:03.320
She broke her leg, but somehow she survived.

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:09.960
The fracture wasn't bad...

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:15.540
...but the trauma from the incident must have damaged her memories...

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:16.970
Damage?

00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:21.750
It seems that she doesn't remember portions of what happened during the night of the fire.

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:28.510
They believed that it was only temporary, and some catalyst was needed to recover her memories.

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:33.460
But, because of that, the police suspected her.

00:12:36.590 --> 00:12:41.240
After a while, her fracture healed, and she started going to school.

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:43.810
But, she became a completely different person.

00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:48.250
After entering high school, she calmed down a lot.

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:51.590
But, during Year 3 of middle school she almost never talked to anyone.

00:12:51.590 --> 00:12:54.640
And the violin she played everyday; she no longer...

00:12:55.780 --> 00:12:56.830
Why...?

00:12:57.720 --> 00:12:59.880
Why didn't you ever tell me?!

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:02.540
Is there anything you could do even if I told you?!

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:09.180
I... I couldn't do a thing!

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:12.220
I didn't do a thing for her!

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:27.140
<i>Is there anything you could do even if I told you?!</i>

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:30.020
<i>I... I couldn't do a thing!</i>

00:13:30.020 --> 00:13:31.880
<i>I didn't do a thing for her!</i>

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:33.920
What's the matter?

00:13:35.550 --> 00:13:37.160
Yuzuki-sensei?

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:39.910
You look rather depressed.

00:13:42.490 --> 00:13:44.730
This seems rather serious.

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:46.380
Here.

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:52.600
Sweet things are good for you if you're feeling down.

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:57.700
Hey, what is it?

00:13:57.700 --> 00:14:01.340
This isn't the first time I've given you caramel, right?

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:04.260
Sensei, can I ask you something?

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:07.930
Anything other than my three sizes.

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:11.330
Why do you give us caramel?

00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:18.880
Both of my parents work.

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:23.910
When I was young, there would be no one at home when I got back.

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:28.050
And the only thing left on the table was my pocket money.

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:30.720
It was telling me something like, "Please use this today."

00:14:31.650 --> 00:14:37.020
My friends told me stuff like, use it for whatever you want.

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:42.380
But, what I wanted was for Mom to say, "Welcome back."

00:14:42.380 --> 00:14:47.080
And then have an afternoon snack with her.

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:53.500
But, part of the household was my grandmother, and she was always sick and in hospital.

00:14:53.500 --> 00:15:00.430
Even though I was still a kid, somehow, I understood the plight of my mom and dad.

00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:05.340
I couldn't be demanding. I figured the natural course of action was to stay quiet.

00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:10.390
So, I gave myself my own afternoon snack.

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:12.990
Give yourself your own?

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:16.670
Yep. It was something like play-acting.

00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:20.300
In a way, I was pretending to be a mother.

00:15:20.300 --> 00:15:24.110
"Yuzu-chan, welcome home. 
Today's afternoon snack is donuts."

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:27.360
"Yay! I love donuts."

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:30.660
"Then, eat with Mommy, okay?"

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:33.360
Would be how I pretended alone.

00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:36.910
Ah, you must be thinking that I was a gloomy kid, didn't you?

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:38.880
No, of course not.

00:15:39.320 --> 00:15:41.860
Well, it's okay. It's true after all.

00:15:43.340 --> 00:15:48.200
But, while I was doing that, I noticed something.

00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:52.980
You know, like ice cream or sweet buns; you can't buy them in quantity with pocket money, right?

00:15:52.980 --> 00:15:56.400
So, I wouldn't be able to give myself an afternoon snack very often, right?

00:15:56.400 --> 00:16:00.150
But, a box of caramels contains many pieces.

00:16:00.150 --> 00:16:03.920
So, if I take them one at a time, I'd be able to give myself an afternoon snack all the time, right?

00:16:05.070 --> 00:16:09.250
"You worked hard on your math drills today, so here's a piece of caramel."

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:13.050
"You were able to vault over five boxes, so here's another."

00:16:13.730 --> 00:16:15.130
Something like that.

00:16:15.130 --> 00:16:18.680
That means, you only gave it to yourself at the start?

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:23.380
Yeah. I only started giving them to others during high school I think.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:29.080
I guess playing house at that age would be kinda silly.

00:16:29.080 --> 00:16:33.130
But, rewarding myself became a habit.

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:35.890
I always carry a box with me wherever I go.

00:16:36.900 --> 00:16:42.430
Then one day, while I was passing through this park on the way back from school...

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:46.150
...there was a boy practicing hip circles on the horizontal bars over there.

00:16:47.550 --> 00:16:52.490
I think he was in Year 2 or 3 of elementary school.

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:57.990
I've forgotten his face, but he did leave a big impression on me.

00:16:57.990 --> 00:17:02.640
No matter how many times he failed, he kept on trying to do a hip circle.

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:05.220
Seeing that, some of his spirit seemed to have rubbed off on me.

00:17:05.220 --> 00:17:11.220
Before I knew it, I was cheering from my heart, "Do your best! Almost! Keep it up!"

00:17:11.220 --> 00:17:15.360
But, just as he almost had it, he ran out of steam.

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:17.350
Cheer up and try once more.

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:27.410
And that's when you gave a caramel...

00:17:27.410 --> 00:17:30.830
He rebelled at first.

00:17:30.830 --> 00:17:36.070
Well, that's a given. It is kinda odd to receive caramel from a girl you don't know.

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:40.980
But, after eating the caramel, he had the most cheerful face.

00:17:40.980 --> 00:17:45.500
Huh? But you said that you didn't remember what he looked like.

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:48.540
I remember that he was making a cheerful face though.

00:17:57.970 --> 00:18:00.550
So, do you feel a little better now?

00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:02.200
Yep.

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:08.750
Onee-chan, I'm gonna give it another shot.

00:18:12.850 --> 00:18:16.440
After giving me such a cheerful face, I was really happy too.

00:18:16.870 --> 00:18:22.660
Ever since then, I'd give caramel to those who work hard or are feeling down.

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:28.460
At first, when I was in school, I only gave them to friends, under-classmen and acquaintances.

00:18:28.740 --> 00:18:35.250
You know, a strange girl giving out sweets; I didn't want parents to misunderstand and create a scene.

00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:39.950
So, in a way, the work I do now is like a calling.

00:18:39.950 --> 00:18:44.340
Because, at work, I can reward hardworking kids...

00:18:44.340 --> 00:18:47.480
...to encourage them without any worry.

00:18:49.750 --> 00:18:52.240
Sensei, I'm going to give it a shot.

00:19:04.590 --> 00:19:06.620
<i>Is there anything you could do even if I told you?!</i>

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:08.820
<i>I don't know.</i>

00:19:08.820 --> 00:19:12.410
<i>I don't know what to do or what I can do.</i>

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:15.750
<i>But, something has to be done.</i>

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:17.470
<i>I have to try!</i>

00:19:31.430 --> 00:19:34.190
What did you call me out here for?

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:36.950
I saw the contents of the mail box.

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:40.770
I heard about the fire as well.

00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:44.540
I'm sorry.

00:19:45.090 --> 00:19:48.760
I never knew that you were in such pain.

00:19:49.350 --> 00:19:52.460
What's the point of saying it now?

00:19:53.410 --> 00:19:57.810
You weren't there when I needed you most!

00:19:57.810 --> 00:20:01.870
Don't you dare apologise to me now!

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:03.300
Wait!

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:04.320
Let go of me!

00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:06.180
Nanaka, I'm not done talking!

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:08.420
There's nothing left to talk about!

00:20:08.420 --> 00:20:09.390
Nanaka!

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:13.700
After hearing about the fire, are you planning to show me pity?

00:20:13.700 --> 00:20:15.480
It's too late!

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:20.040
After all, you probably forgot about me after going to that school far away!

00:20:20.470 --> 00:20:23.850
You don't even know how much I suffered back then!

00:20:23.850 --> 00:20:26.720
And you were probably having fun with your new friends there, right?!

00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:35.510
You didn't...

00:20:36.280 --> 00:20:38.180
...even remember me.

00:20:38.730 --> 00:20:41.050
And also...

00:20:43.250 --> 00:20:47.310
